# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
#
# ASan/UBSan/LSan suppressions for the nightly `asan` lane (issue #702,
# docs/specs/memory-model-v1.md section 10).
#
# Format: one entry per line, `interceptor:pattern`, preceded by a `#` comment line that gives the
# reason. The sanitizer runtime ignores blank lines and `#` comments.
#
# POLICY - read before adding a line:
#   * Tessera's own code is NEVER suppressed here. If our code trips ASan, UBSan or LSan, that is a
#     finding to report and fix, not to silence. The lane exists to surface it.
#   * Only a third-party library may be listed, and only with a reason that names the library, the
#     report it emits and why the report is not ours to fix.
#
# CURRENT STATE: empty. The full ctest set, including the lavapipe GPU suites, runs under
# ASan+UBSan with no suppressions. Everything the first full run reported was Tessera's own code and
# was fixed rather than suppressed. Leak suppressions live in `lsan.supp`, not here: ASan's parser
# rejects the `leak:` type, so a shared file would make every test abort with "failed to parse
# suppressions".
